cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SourceTrace in research or reporting, please cite it as below."
title: "SourceTrace: follow a statistic back to where it came from"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: BurnMeDown
version: 0.5.1
date-released: 2026-11-17
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/BurnMeDown-AI/SourceTrace"
url: "https://burnmedown-ai.github.io/SourceTrace/"
keywords:
  - fact-checking
  - statistics
  - citations
  - misinformation
  - provenance
abstract: >-
  SourceTrace takes a claim and the page where it appears, follows the page's
  citations hop by hop, checks that each source states that number about that
  topic, and reports where the trail ends.
